  "Question": "\\(A\\) can do a piece of work in \\(9\\) days. \\(B\\) is \\(50\\%\\) more efficient than \\(A.\\) The number of days it takes \\(B\\) to do the same piece of work is:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(13\\dfrac12\\)",
    "B": "\\(4\\dfrac12\\)",
    "C": "\\(6\\)",
    "D": "\\(3\\)",
    "E": "None of these answers"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "Efficiency here means the amount of work completed per day. Being \\(50\\%\\) more efficient means that \\(B\\) completes \\(1+\\frac12=\\frac32\\) times as much work per day as \\(A\\).\n\nThus, in \\(2\\) days, \\(B\\) completes as much work as \\(A\\) completes in \\(3\\) days. The whole job takes \\(A\\) three such \\(3\\)-day portions, since \\(9=3\\cdot3\\). Therefore \\(B\\) needs\n\\[\n3\\cdot2=6\\text{ days},\n\\]\nchoice C.",
